    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d372-a1">

                <pb facs="0509" n="429" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg429"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor de Osma to Mr.
                            Dudley.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1901-07-05"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">July 5, 1901.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: In conformity with my note
                    addressed to your legation on the 21st of last May, in consequence of your
                    excellency’s acceptance of the proposal I made in the said note to arrange the
                    claim of Mr. J. H. Hayball, I have the pleasure to inclose you a check, No.
                    448011, drawn by the public treasury on “El Banco del Peru y Londres,” for the
                    sum of 8,000 soles, in full settlement of the said claim.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. de Osma.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
